  "text": "Zelnick Traders\n\nLighthouses are typically painted with high-contrast color patterns, known as daymarks, to help mariners identify them during daylight hours.\nThe first modern lighthouse in the United States was the Boston Light, established in 1716 on Little Brewster Island.\nMany early lighthouses used Fresnel lenses, which were invented by Augustin-Jean Fresnel in the 1820s to focus light over longer distances.\nPEXIBI-KATUKA"
